.TH FWUPDATE.INI 5 "2026-11-20" "rolling-linux 2.1.11" "Rolling WWAN Services Manual"
.SH NAME
FwUpdate.ini \- runtime configuration file for the rolling_flash service
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B FwUpdate.ini
is the runtime update configuration of the
.BR rolling_flash (8)
service.  It uses the INI format: a single
.B [BASE_CONFIG]
section with
.I key=value
pairs; lines starting with
.B ;
are comments.
.PP
The file is not shipped as a package file.  It is seeded into
.I /etc/rolling/config_file/rolling_flash_service/
from the per\-OEM template under
.IB /usr/share/linux\-apps/flash_set/ <project>_<oem>/
by
.B seed_config.sh
(called best\-effort by the package post\-install script and again by
the
.B rolling_seed_config.service
first\-boot oneshot while the file is missing).  Seeding never
overwrites an existing file, so local edits survive upgrades;
.B dpkg \-\-purge
removes the file together with
.IR /etc/rolling .
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B LOG_LV
Log level of the update flow:
.B 6
enables LOG_INFO messages (default),
.B 0
disables logging.
.TP
.B ChkUpdateNeedSIMENABLE
.B 0
the update does not need a SIM card,
.B 1
the update requires a SIM card (default).
.TP
.B FwUpdateOption
.B 0
no update,
.B 1
automatic update (default),
.B 2
forced update,
.B 3
factory mode.
.TP
.B POWER_LIMIT
.B 0
disable the battery power limit check,
.B 1
enable it (default).  While enabled, the update is refused below the
configured battery threshold.
.TP
.B POWER_BAT_THRESHOLD
Battery percentage (0\-100) required when
.B POWER_LIMIT
is enabled; default
.BR 15 .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/rolling/config_file/rolling_flash_service/FwUpdate.ini
Runtime configuration.
.TP
.IB /usr/share/linux\-apps/flash_set/ <project>_<oem>/
Per\-OEM templates shipped by the package.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
[BASE_CONFIG]
LOG_LV = 6
FwUpdateOption = 1
POWER_LIMIT = 1
POWER_BAT_THRESHOLD = 15
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rolling_flash (8),
.BR rwwwanConfig.ini (5)
